# Character 3D visual policy (design lock)

Status: **locked** (Ruida, 2026-08-17).

## Individual characters (`Char_*`)

| Rule | Lock |
|------|------|
| 3D mesh | **No** per-person StaticMesh / SkeletalMesh for registry characters. Do not model, rig, or spawn named individuals as 3D persons. |
| Animation | **No** 3D skeletal animation for individuals (walk, idle, combat pose, emote on a person pawn). |
| Identity | **2D avatar icon** (persisted in save) + UI text — Character panel, tavern, company, ship **2D outfit slots** (`ship-system.mdc`). |
| Strategic map | **No** `ACharacter` / person Actor. **Not** parented to fleet, city, or ship 3D meshes. Agency through hosts (fleet, company, city logic). |
| Logic | Unchanged: `UCharacterObject` + subsystems; posts on Company / Fleet — see `character-system.mdc`. |

## When person-like expression is needed

Use **other channels first** — do not default to individual 3D:

- UI portraits / icons / panels
- 2D schematic slot anchors (e.g. ship 改装 diagram)
- Host motion on the map (fleet sails; city interaction UI)
- Text, receipts, logs, future illustration or VFX **not** bound to a `Char_*` skeleton

If a feature still feels like it “needs a 3D person,” **stop and discuss with Ruida** before adding assets or Actor types.

## Exception — illustrative aggregates (not designed; may never ship)

| Rule | Lock |
|------|------|
| Scope | **Anonymous mass** 3D **only** for schematic effect — e.g. “a crowd,” “an army unit” as **one** visual mass, **not** mappable to `Char_*` ids. |
| Status | **Not designed.** **Not planned for v0.** **May never be implemented.** |
| Prohibition | Do **not** use this exception for named NPCs, companions, officers, tavern hangers, or any registry character. |
| Implementation | Requires **explicit Ruida decision** + update to this rule **before** art or code. |

## Overturn

Any change to individual 3D / skeletal policy requires an **explicit Ruida decision** and same-change updates to this file and `character-system.mdc` (**Scene & agency**).
